 "result": "Call order at the end of a request (from `brain/` notes; I didn't open the source files):\n\n1. `Tessel.wsgi_entry` — `src/tessel/app.py` (~L1566); runs the request.\n2. `Tessel.run_full_request` — `src/tessel/app.py`; produces the return value.\n3. `Tessel.finalize_request` — `src/tessel/app.py`; calls `make_response`, then `finalize_reply`.\n4. `Tessel.finalize_reply` — `src/tessel/app.py` (~L1394); runs the `after_request` funcs, then calls `persist_session` unless the session is a null session.\n5. `SignedCookieSessionInterface.persist_session` — `src/tessel/sessions.py`. It does one of three things:\n   - Session empty and modified: `response.delete_cookie`.\n   - Session empty and not modified: nothing.\n   - Otherwise: `set_cookie`, when `cookie_needs_write` is true.\n6. Helpers used by `persist_session`, all in `src/tessel/sessions.py`:\n   - `SessionInterface.cookie_needs_write`, `get_expiration_time` and the `get_cookie_*` getters, which read the `SESSION_COOKIE_*` config keys.\n   - `make_signer(app)`, which builds the itsdangerous `URLSafeTimedSerializer`.\n   - `TypedCookieSerializer` (exposed as `session_json_serializer`) in `src/tessel/json/tag.py`, which encodes the payload.",
